an><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-concurrency-ts t-mark-ts\">(concurrency TS)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  produces a future that is ready immediately and holds the given exception <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::make_ready_future","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. If std::decay_t<T> is std::reference_wrapper<X>, then the type V is X&, otherwise, V is std::decay_t<T>."},{"label":"Return value","note":"A std::experimental::future associated with the shared state that is created."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"make_exceptional_future","note":"produces a future that is ready immediately and holds the given exception"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":116,"codeBlockCount":0}
